LICENSING FOR THIS REPOSITORY
=============================

This repository has two kinds of content and they are not under the same terms.


1. THE STATISTICS CANADA DATA
-----------------------------

Everything staged under data/, and every file published as an asset of a
release of this repository, is Statistics Canada material made available under
the STATISTICS CANADA OPEN LICENCE.

The required statement for this material, reproduced exactly as it appears in
this repository's README:

    Adapted from Statistics Canada, 2021 Census Geographic Attribute File (92-151-X), 2016 and 2021 Census Correspondence Files (92-156-X), and Table 17-10-0155-01, 2011/2016/2021 reference years. This does not constitute an endorsement by Statistics Canada of this product. Licence: Statistics Canada Open Licence.

Anyone redistributing this material, in whole or in part, must carry that
statement with it and must comply with the licence in full.

THE AUTHORITATIVE TEXT OF THE LICENCE IS NOT REPRODUCED HERE, DELIBERATELY.
Statistics Canada publishes it, and a paraphrase or a remembered copy of a
licence is worse than a pointer to the real one. Read it at Statistics Canada's
own site:

    https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/terms-conditions/open-licence

(An older path, https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/reference/licence, has also served
this licence. If the two ever disagree, the text Statistics Canada is currently
publishing governs -- not this file.)

Among the licence's terms, and the reason the statement above is worded as it
is: a product that ADAPTS Statistics Canada information must not be annotated
in any way that could be read as an endorsement by Statistics Canada, and must
not imply exclusive access to, or an exclusive distribution arrangement for,
Statistics Canada information.


2. THIS REPOSITORY'S OWN CODE
-----------------------------

The workflow, the scripts under scripts/, and the tests under tests/ are not
Statistics Canada material and are not covered by the licence above. They are
the work of this repository's owner.

No licence has been chosen for them. Until one is, no permissions beyond those
GitHub's Terms of Service grant for public repositories should be assumed.


3. WHAT IS NOT COVERED BY EITHER SECTION
----------------------------------------

data/blocks/, data/mapworthy-blocks-sample.ndjson.gz and
data/mapworthy-block-layer-meta.json are derived from Statistics Canada's
public cartographic boundary web service and are therefore Statistics Canada
material under section 1. They are not produced by the workflow in this
repository and are not published as release assets by it.
